{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Implementation pushed for review: Gerrit change 1916 (commit 7ad468f867, Change-Id Iffdc5d03b43bc68e0e42fec2e820aa3a1d0ea72d), branch r3-composition-gate off origin/main 0b851c8103.\n\nR3's FIRST RUN on the real tree enumerated exactly 7 hits across 2 functions, with ZERO false positives anywhere else in src/ + scripts/ (the riskiest-assumption check from the plan): __main__.py:338-351 read_tree/rm_cached/write_tree/commit_tree/update_ref, and reconcile_helpers.py:226/246 add/commit. Both took a durable reasoned function-level marker as planned; no debt baseline, no allowlist file.\n\nLocal gates: make lint exit 0 (complexity ratchet active=49 new=0 increased=0); make typecheck exit 0 over 568 files; tests/unit/test_raw_git_write_lint.py 49 passed (up from 42 — 7 new R3 tests plus the parametrized seam-file case and the repo-tree regression); tests/unit/rebar_reconciler 2945 passed; scripts/check_raw_git_writes.py exits 0 on the tree and --report lists all 7 seam-composition hits with their reasons.\n\nOne plan detail corrected during implementation: an empty binding set is NOT sufficient to disable R3 inside the seam files, because the module NAME alone binds a receiver. _SeamBindings therefore carries an explicit 'enabled' flag that the seam-internal files switch off. Caught by the parametrized sanctioned-entry test, which failed on the first implementation pass."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787174610611195001,"uuid":"93727812-e7df-4af1-aa8e-402e4fe75782"}